"answer": "The emails regarding Q2 budget revisions highlight several key developments. Oliver Grant (Project Manager) reported that capital expenditure projects for Q2, including the new office building and IT infrastructure upgrade, came in 10% over budget, necessitating financial projection adjustments. Henry Scott (CEO) instructed Jordan to prepare for the Q2 earnings call, specifically to outline the impact of these budget revisions and discuss the updated profit forecast. Diana Wells (Chief Auditor) noted that the upcoming Q2 financial audit will require accurate records of these recent budget revisions. Finally, Karen Smith (CFO) shared the revised Q2 budget, which includes shifting funds to emerging market bonds, and updated the Q2 profit forecast to $9.378 million, a 3.5% increase from previous estimates."
